cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AcousticMonster: reproducible acoustic localisation and Bayesian calibration"
type: software
version: 1.0
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/example/AcousticMonster"
abstract: >-
  Research code reproducing the E1-E7 experiments: speed-of-sound sensitivity,
  legacy-LMS divergence prediction, delay RMSE vs echo SNR, sovereign Bayesian
  calibration, GPLA-12 numerical robustness, safety/security checks and
  performance measurement. Datasets are pinned to a commit and sha256-verified.
keywords:
  - acoustics
  - localisation
  - Bayesian neural network
  - pulse-echo
  - reproducibility
